<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nagda (Rajasthan)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nagda is an ancient town beside Bagela Lake near Kailashpuri, about 20 km north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>. It was the early capital of the Guhila rulers of Mewar until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iltutmish">Iltutmish</a> sacked it in the 1220s. Its ruined temples include the richly carved Sahastra Bahu temples of the tenth or eleventh century, popularly called Sas-Bahu, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ekalinga">Eklingji</a> temple stands close by.</p></div>
